<article class="env-lemma" id="01UA">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01UA">Lemma <span data-tag="01UA">29.26.10</span>.</a> A flat morphism locally of finite presentation is universally open. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Lemmas <a href="/tag/03HV" data-tag="03HV">29.26.9</a> and Lemma <a href="/tag/01U1" data-tag="01U1">29.24.2</a> above. We can also argue directly as follows. 
    <p>
      Let $f : X \to S$ be flat and locally of finite presentation. By Lemmas <a href="/tag/01U9" data-tag="01U9">29.26.8</a> and <a href="/tag/01TS" data-tag="01TS">29.22.4</a> any base change of $f$ is flat and locally of finite presentation. Hence it suffices to show $f$ is open. To show $f$ is open it suffices to show that we may cover $X$ by open affines $X = \bigcup U_ i$ such that $U_ i \to S$ is open. We may cover $X$ by affine opens $U_ i \subset X$ such that each $U_ i$ maps into an affine open $V_ i \subset S$ and such that the induced ring map $\mathcal{O}_ S(V_ i) \to \mathcal{O}_ X(U_ i)$ is flat and of finite presentation (Lemmas <a href="/tag/01U5" data-tag="01U5">29.26.3</a> and <a href="/tag/01TQ" data-tag="01TQ">29.22.2</a>). Then $U_ i \to V_ i$ is open by Algebra, Proposition <a href="/tag/00I1" data-tag="00I1">10.41.8</a> and the proof is complete. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>